{
  "$comment": "What a use-case node (Tighten Episode, Chapters, Trailer) hands on from what it holds, on BOTH engines: the editor's readers (frontend/src/__tests__/use-case-engine-parity.test.ts) and the server's (backend/src/services/workflow-engine/__tests__/use-case-engine-parity.test.ts) are each held to the values here, so they agree and cannot agree on the wrong thing. `shape` names a saved state in use-case-output-shapes.json. `handOn`: what a wire from `pip` (null: no pip) carries to a generic consumer, `value` null when it carries nothing; on `json` it is the plan with the person's review applied (a clip-set edit of a chapter list included), and a plan held as null is nothing, never the text \"null\". `prompt`: a `json` pip wired into a text or prompt input (the canvas accepts each of these wires) lands its plan as the consumer's prompt (never as a video, whatever the node's episode is), `prompt` null when nothing lands. `jsonReaders`: Extract Field, JSON Process and filter-list wired to the `json` pip read the same reviewed plan. `fanOut`: an Each wire from the `json` pip into a Prompt fans out over these items (null: no fan-out) — the reviewed list, exactly what filter-list reads: a dropped chapter never runs, and one kept chapter is no fan-out; a plan that is not a list (Tighten's EDL) never fans out, not even over the node's saved episode takes. `listModes`: a wire from the `json` pip in an item mode (`item:N`) into a Prompt picks the Nth item of that same reviewed list; a plan that is not a list (Tighten's EDL) is handed on whole, never one of the node's video takes.",
